From: MilkFlint <milkflint@localhost>
Date: Thu, 19 Nov 2026 16:40:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] net/sched: sch_cake: small savings on the packet path

Each keeps what CAKE does, but for the start of autorate-ingress's
estimate (9):

1. cake_clear_tin() returns at once for a tin with nothing queued.
   autorate-ingress reconfigures up to four times a second, each time
   looking at every queue of every tin not in use, and cake_reset() at
   every queue of all eight tins.
2. Plain cake: cake_dequeue() returns without reading the clock when
   nothing is queued.
3. cake_drop() takes the time cake_enqueue() read.
4. quantum_div[] is filled in once, at module init, not by each
   cake_init().
5. cake_overhead(): a GSO packet whose last segment is as full as the
   others is charged with one cake_calc_overhead() for all of them.
6. cake_set_rate(): fls64() for the shift loop.
7. cake_mq_share(): the floor's division only where it can be above the
   share. With no more used than everyone's sparse flows, the share has
   more of the rate to share out than the floor, between fewer bids.
8. The ACK filter: in its conservative mode it drops an ACK only once it
   has found two it may drop, both pure ACKs, so with fewer than two
   queued it doesn't read the queue; and the new packet's headers are
   read once, not again for the filter.
9. autorate-ingress's capacity estimate is kept only while it's on (it
   was added up, then thrown away, for every packet), and starts afresh
   when it's turned on.

KUnit: an empty tin cleared as before, a GSO packet's charge with and
without a short last segment, the shift against the loop, the share
against the floor's division always made, the ACK filter's skipped reads
against upstream's filter, autorate-ingress turned on.

